  "reading": {
   "title": "Linda's work schedule",
   "text": "Hafsa's neighbor Linda works at a big supermarket. She has a full-time job, but she doesn't work from nine to five. Her shift starts at two in the afternoon and finishes at ten at night. She works five days a week, from Tuesday to Saturday.\n\nLinda doesn't work on Sundays and Mondays. On those days, she rests and cleans her house. Her boss, Mr. Green, is a good manager. He doesn't ask the workers to stay late, and he pays every two weeks.\n\nLinda doesn't like the late hours very much. She gets home at ten thirty, and she is tired. She doesn't eat dinner late, so she has a small snack at work during her break. At the supermarket, the workers wear a green uniform. Linda says, \"I don't love the shift, but I love my coworkers.\"",
   "glossary": [
