   "title": "A new job at the school cafeteria",
   "script": [
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "Hafsa, I have good news. The cafeteria needs a part-time worker."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Hafsa",
     "text": "Really? What is the schedule?"
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "The shift starts at ten and finishes at two. It's four hours a day."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Hafsa",
     "text": "Do I work on weekends?"
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "No, you don't. The school doesn't open on weekends."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Hafsa",
     "text": "That's good. My son Emre doesn't go to school on Saturdays, so I stay home with him."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "You also have a short break at noon. The cafeteria doesn't close during lunch, so the workers take turns."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Hafsa",
     "text": "Do I wear a uniform?"
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "Yes, a blue apron. The school gives it to you."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Hafsa",
     "text": "And my boss? Who is the manager?"
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "Ms. Davis. She doesn't shout, and she helps new workers."
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Hafsa",
     "text": "Perfect. When do I start?"
    },
    {
     "speaker": "Mr. Brown",
     "text": "Next Monday. Come at nine thirty, please."
    }
